w include  all-out attack and park the boss dead  ball situations now include tactics  modifiers or you can decide to play as  an outfielder and ask to receive the  ball pitches get worn in as the game  progresses jerseys get wet and muddy you  can pick snowy weather if you want but  they forgot to put the orange ball in  the demo so only do it if you want to  lose sight of the default white one  every fight  seconds oh and the dead fish is back  yeah dead fish the camera cuts away to  these nice vanity shots a lot more the  half time whistle and idling in the menu  music kicks off this nice slow-mo high  contrast demo reel menus have been given  a facelift to with player stats and  photos more upfront they even stuck in  photos from martin Tyler and allen Smith  oddly enough specific details on player  injuries it used to be in the squad menu  don't appear anymore which makes it  harder to decide whether you should take  off Xavi once he's randomly walked off  the pitch after being tackled why are  you waving at me I are you injured are  you badly injured I'll bloody holly's  walk back on so it's not without its  idiosyncrasies but the on pitch action  in 15 does seem better than last year's  at least in terms of modes I guess we'll  have to wait and see the bizarrely  omitted tournament mode and guest play  will be returning it's not sure about  unripe friendlies though but you can  expect a shed load more ultimate team  stuff and based on all these menu  changes in the demo hopefully a better  interface for career mode thanks for  watching those are my thoughts on a  course we'll have a review of p215 on  gamespot com once it's out what do you  guys think let us know in the comment
 

